<<~ ahu slot=`#/per-red`>>

!! Per red

# ''sibling-system-canon-admin (node-a).'' Test wrong, plus mixed code wording. The realm's refusal says "house canon"; the sibling-face refusals in `operator-daemon-behavior.ts` still said "system canon", although they gate `isHouseCanonBag`. Code: all three kahu-reach refusals now say "house canon". Test: assertions and title say house canon. Filename kept: `tools/e2e-shard-weights.json` points at it.
# ''container-target (cli-mesh).'' Test wrong. Each `meme get` in `host-bridge-real-docker.test.ts` (lines 91, 92, 105, 125) now passes `--bag lares`. The stand-in `node` script scans every argument for `exit:N` / `sleep`, so the walks still work. The law stays as it was: no exception and no `intentional-bare-refusal` marker (these are not refusal vectors).
# ''born-with-cap (web-tw5).'' Test wrong, code right. A top-level CREATE has no inner bag, so `gateRoutedVerb` never asks Kahu about it. That means `kahuReachClearedAtGate` never cleared a CREATE. `createHouseCanon` checks the `kahuReach` source itself, and with none it treats the caller as a stranger: `readsFloor`, `count: 0`. The test now passes the steward's own `kahuReach: await kahuHand()`. The steward's answer then counts the realm document's titles (1). Title renamed to "house canon … steward".
# ''share-verbs (web-tw5).'' Test wrong. `VerbRefusal` carries `reason` across the house (about 66 test reads use it; `code` belongs to other error classes). Both refusals in the test now match on `reason`.
# ''seed-census K15 (witness).'' Some of each:
#* Line 425 (`siblingSlotsOf`: `vesselDid`/`mintedByHex` = the PUBLIC place key for a sibling face's resolver) was new this span. It took one of the row's 3 counted slots, so the older line 1788 showed up as open. I restructured it: `LitFaceSlotSpec` now takes `atomKey`, and `litFaceSlotDocs` builds minted-by and the DID from it, the same way the worn face labels its own slots. Reason: a sibling's binding records (`minted-by` in the worn face's daemon doc) would otherwise carry the place key, which links that face to the place.
#* 1474 (`share-apply` salt): classified. The salt only has to differ per vessel ("reads alike on no other vessel"). The flag sits in the vessel's own control document, which no face reads, so a public per-vessel value does the job.
#* 1788 (face-owner mount comparison): classified. The old reason text already named it.
#* The census row now reads count 4 (367 faceless floor label, 466 floor label a lit face lifts, 1474 salt, 1788 mount comparison). Its reason no longer names the retired boot place check.

<<~/ahu>>

