!! Proven green alone
seed-census.test.mjs 9/9 · lares-cli container-target 8/8 · tw5 share-verbs, born-with-cap 13/13, catalog-split-create 9/9 · keyhive lit-face-slots 4/4 · node sibling-system-canon-admin 1/1. Typecheck green for keyhive, tw5, node and cli. A full `pnpm -r build` plus stamp ran green in the worktree, with a scratch LAR_ROOT and no LAR_BAGS. `git status` showed no dirt under bags/ or wikis/; I did not run the tree-clean-witness script itself. host-bridge-real-docker was edited but not run (it needs `LARES_REAL_DOCKER=1`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/possible-product-bugs`>>

!! Possible product bugs
* `kahuReachClearedAtGate` vs `createHouseCanon`: a composition cleared at the gate with no `kahuReach` source answers even the steward's CREATE with `readsFloor`. That is correct today, because `deriveRoutedCap` sends house-canon CREATE to the daemon bag, which carries the source. If CREATE ever reaches a wiki island, the steward would read as a stranger. The option's doc ("asked the Kahu predicate for every system bag this verb names") still says "system".
* In this span's source, "system canon" still names both the lares+lararium core and house canon in many comments (kahu-canon-reach.ts, action-handler.ts, verb-local-dispatch.ts). Only refusals were changed here.
* Sibling slot resolvers write binding records into the worn face's daemon store (`daemonStore: ctx.composite`). Only device slots reach this today. If a sibling ever resolves a non-device slot, its binding rows would land in the worn face's daemon doc. Worth a look.
* No CHANGELOG entry for the `LitFaceSlotSpec.atomKey` change.

<<~/ahu>>

